            "text": "### 5. Why Do We Care? (How They Are Used)",
            "start": 2433,
            "end": 2475
          },
          {
            "id": "p35",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Why does this matter outside of a chemistry test? Isotopes are actually super useful in the real world:",
            "start": 2476,
            "end": 2579
          },
          {
            "id": "p36",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "*   **Carbon Dating:** Remember Carbon-14? Because it’s radioactive, it slowly breaks down at a steady pace over thousands of years. Archeologists measure how much Carbon-14 is left in ancient fossils or mummy bones to figure out exactly how old they are!",
            "start": 2581,
            "end": 2836
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "Accurately summarizes the principle of carbon dating using C-14 decay in organic archaeological specimens.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
